Z||000004||Cooter||10-31-1999||11:16 PM||||The price for the Holley throttle body in the Fiero Store is way too much. Go to Holley's website and find the part number and then call Summit or Jegs. They can get the part for a lot less.||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||11-01-1999||03:00 PM||||84-86 Fiero 4 cyl uses the GM 300 series TBI. The Holley unit is a modified 300 design with a bigger main bore & butterfly.<P>The 87+ Fiero 4 cyl uses GM's 700 series TBI. This unit is a completely diferant design. It is not a direct swap part. You would need to change linkages, manifold, and electrical connectors to use it. Even then I'm not sure it would work right with the older ECM.||||reg||1
Z||000006||88formula||11-01-1999||04:50 PM||||Its not worth the trouble or the cost. I was just curious,thaks for the info anyway.||||reg||1
Z||000007||WKDFIRO||11-05-1999||08:39 PM||||Best thing I did for my 87 four cyl Fiero. Throw away that weak excuse for a manifold and get the Hooker tri-Y header. I never had a problem with smog with it, (it has a spot for the 02 sensor) but got so much more out of the engine. PROBLEM: the way my header was bent on the bottom it came too close to the starter solenoid, no matter how much protection I was changing starters every 6 months. Car was destroyed from behind before I could take it to the exhaust shop to fix it. I don't make any hp guesses but it is just so much better for flow its scary. Oh, dont forget to take out the intake muffler for better intake flow when you replace it with a straight tube!<BR>||||reg||1
